    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43782" root="&#xA;                        ميل&#xA;                    " body-key="m1">
                        
                            6
                            <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَمَايَلَ فِى مِشْيَتِهِ</span></b> 
                         [<i>He affected an inclining
of his body,</i> or <i>a bending,</i> or <i>he inclined his body,</i>
or <i>bent, from side to side, in his gait;</i> a meaning
well known, and still common]; (S;) syn. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَثَنَّى</span>.
(Har, p. 269.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  See <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَزَايُغٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَمَايَلَتْ فِى</span>
                        <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِشْيَتِهَا</span> and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَمَيَّلَتْ</span></b>  signify the same. (TA.)
― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَمَايَلَ إِلَى الشَّىْءِ</span>; and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَنْ طَرِيقِهِ</span>: <i>i. q.</i>
                        <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَجَانَفَ</span>
[<i>He affected a deviation,</i> or <i>purposely deviated
from his course,</i> &amp;c.] (TA in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جنف</span>.)

